# Exact downstream request bytes, in order (step dividers)

### step 1: POST http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/api-call (control: direct api-call hits mock)
POST /v0/management/api-call HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 68


{"method":"GET","url":"http://host.docker.internal:20999/v1/models"}

### step 2: POST http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/api-call (dead socks5 -> transport engaged)
POST /v0/management/api-call HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 103


{"method":"GET","url":"http://host.docker.internal:20999/v1/models","proxy_url":"socks5://127.0.0.1:9"}

### step 3: POST http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/api-call (ftp:// invalid proxy_url)
POST /v0/management/api-call HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1
Content-Type: application/json
